ird and pipe rectangles; ground/ceiling are hard limits","Score increments exactly once when a pipe passes the bird's x and hasn't been scored yet","Game over state freezes updates except allowing reset","Reset returns bird to initial position, clears pipes, resets score and game-over flag","Configuration validation prevents nonsensical parameters (e.g., negative gravity, zero gap height)","All updates are driven by a supplied dt to remain deterministic in tests"],"Product Goals":["Deliver a clean, testable core game logic with deterministic behavior","Provide a small runtime demo that safely starts and exits","Keep architecture modular with clear boundaries for RNG/time and domain"],"User Stories":["As a player, I want the bird to rise when I flap and then fall due to gravity.","As a player, I want pipes to move toward the bird with gaps I can pass through.","As a player, I want the game to end when I hit a pipe or go out of bounds.","As a player, I want my score to increase when I successfully pass a pipe.","As a player, I want to be able to reset the game to try again."],"Competitive Analysis":["Original Flappy Bird: iconic mechanics, simple control, constant difficulty curve","Minimal console clones: often monolithic code, weak separation of logic and runtime","Academic demos of physics-based 2D games: good separation and determinism for testing","Indie clones with procedural generation: varied gap positions and speeds","Game programming tutorials: useful but often lack deterministic tests"],"Competitive Quadrant Chart":"quadrantChart
