1) CMakeLists.txt [Alex]
- Define project with C++17, two executables: flappy_demo (src/Main.cpp + src/*.cpp) and tests (tests/test_main.cpp). Enable CTest and add test that runs the single test target.

2) include/Random.h [Bob]
- Declare canonical RNG boundary.
- API: class IRandom { virtual ~IRandom(); virtual double nextUnit()=0; }.
- API: class LcgRandom : public IRandom { explicit LcgRandom(uint64_t seed); double nextUnit() override; uint64_t nextUint64(); }.
- Semantics: nextUnit returns [0,1) deterministically; nextUint64 returns the raw sequence.

3) src/Random.cpp [Bob]
- Implement LCG with 64-bit state: state = (a*state + c) mod 2^64, standard constants (e.g., a=6364136223846793005, c=1). Convert to double in [0,1).
- Validate via simple non-throwing behavior; no external deps.

4) include/GameConfig.h [Bob]
- Declare struct GameConfig with gameplay constants: worldWidth, worldHeight, gravity, flapImpulse, maxFallSpeed, pipeSpeed, pipeWidth, pipeGapHeight, pipeSpawnInterval, birdX, birdWidth, birdHeight.
- Provide static GameConfig Default(); void validate() const; equality comparators not required.
- Document error behavior: validate throws std::invalid_argument on invalid values.

5) src/GameConfig.cpp [Bob]
- Implement Default() with reasonable deterministic values (e.g., width=400, height=300, gravity=900 px/s^2, flapImpulse=300 px/s, maxFallSpeed=600 px/s, pipeSpeed=80 px/s, pipeWidth=40 px, pipeGapHeight=120 px, pipeSpawnInterval=1.5 s, birdX=80 px, birdWidth=24 px, birdHeight=18 px).
- Implement validate(): ensure all positives where applicable, birdX within world.

6) include/Bird.h [Eve]
- Declare class Bird with private double y_, v_; non-owning constants taken from GameConfig.
- API: Bird(double y0, double v0);
- void flap(const GameConfig& cfg);
- void update(double dt, const GameConfig& cfg);
- double y() const; double velocity() const; double top(const GameConfig& cfg) const; double bottom(const GameConfig& cfg) const;
- void reset(double y0);
- Semantics: flap adds upward impulse to velocity (negative up or positive up depending convention; choose positive up and apply gravity downward), update clamps within world bounds and caps fall speed.

7) src/Bird.cpp [Eve]
- Implement physics: v_ += flapImpulse on flap; update: v_ -= gravity*dt; clamp v_ >= -maxFallSpeed if using up-positive; y_ += v_*dt; clamp y_ within [birdHeight/2, worldHeight - birdHeight/2].
- Provide top/bottom using birdHeight.

8) include/Pipe.h [Eve]
- Declare struct Pipe { double x; double gapY; bool scored; }.
- API: Pipe(double x0, double gapY0);
- void update(double dt, const GameConfig& cfg);
- bool isOffscreen(const GameConfig& cfg) const;
- bool hasPassedBird(double birdX, const GameConfig& cfg) const;
- bool collidesWithBird(double birdX, double birdTop, double birdBottom, const GameConfig& cfg) const;
- Semantics: gapY is center of gap; collision checks if bird rectangle overlaps either top or bottom pipe rectangle.

9) src/Pipe.cpp [Eve]
- Implement horizontal movement: x -= pipeSpeed*dt.
- isOffscreen: x + pipeWidth < 0.
- hasPassedBird: (x + pipeWidth) < birdX.
- collidesWithBird: compute pipe rectangles: top: [x, x+pipeWidth] x [0, gapY - gapHeight/2]; bottom: [x, x+pipeWidth] x [gapY + gapHeight/2, worldHeight]; check overlap with bird rectangle [birdX - birdWidth/2, birdX + birdWidth/2] x [birdTop, birdBottom].

10) include/GameState.h [Alex]
- Declare class GameState encapsulating Bird, pipes, score, gameOver, timeSinceLastPipe.
- API: explicit GameState(const GameConfig& cfg);
- void reset();
- void flap();
- void update(double dt, IRandom& rng);
- int score() const; bool gameOver() const;
- const std::vector<Pipe>& pipes() const; double birdY() const; double birdTop() const; double birdBottom() const;
- Semantics: update advances bird and pipes if not gameOver; spawns new pipes when timer exceeds spawn interval with gapY determined via rng; scoring when pipes pass bird; set gameOver on collision or out-of-bounds.

11) src/GameState.cpp [Alex]
- Implement constructor with initial bird centered vertically and cleared pipes.
- Implement spawn logic: gapY = clamp((rng.nextUnit()*(worldHeight - pipeGapHeight)) + pipeGapHeight/2), x = worldWidth.
- Implement per-tick: decrement timer, spawn as needed; update pipes; remove offscreen pipes; scoring set once per pipe via hasPassedBird; collision detection via collidesWithBird.

12) include/GameEngine.h [Alex]
- Declare class GameEngine that owns GameConfig and IRandom (via unique_ptr) and a GameState instance.
- API: explicit GameEngine(GameConfig cfg, std::unique_ptr<IRandom> rng);
- void reset();
- void flap();
- void step(double dt);
- int score() const; bool isGameOver() const; double birdY() const; const std::vector<Pipe>& pipes() const; const GameConfig& config() const;
- Semantics: thin wrapper delegating to GameState with provided RNG; guards calls when gameOver.

13) src/GameEngine.cpp [Alex]
- Implement all methods; validate config via cfg.validate() in constructor; on reset() rebuild GameState.

14) src/Main.cpp [Alex]
- Non-interactive demo: construct GameEngine with GameConfig::Default() and LcgRandom(seed=42); run a short simulation for ~5 seconds with fixed dt (e.g., 0.02 s), apply flaps at deterministic intervals (e.g., every 0.6 s); print final score and game over state; exit.
- No loops that wait for input; no graphics.

